<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Qara Yusuf</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1420">1420</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Qara Yusuf was the leader of the Qara Qoyunlu <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmen">Turkmen</a> confederation from 1388 to 1420. Driven out by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a>, he returned after Timur's death, killed the Jalayirid sultan Ahmad in 1410 and took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabriz">Tabriz</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a>, making the Qara Qoyunlu the leading power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>. In 1409 he also ended Artuqid rule at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mardin">Mardin</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/qara-yusuf.jpg" alt="Qara Yusuf" width="252" height="383" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 15th century artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Qara_Yusuf_enthroned,_15th_century.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
